1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,084
Host: Welcome to KC Desk Notes. Today we are unpacking one fresh research report and the question it raises.

2
00:00:06,444 --> 00:00:15,221
Host: We’re looking at a fresh initiation of coverage on Kioxia Holdings today. The title is a bit punchy: “Peak is not here yet.” What’s the big idea?

3
00:00:15,581 --> 00:00:23,383
Guest: Right. The report argues that the market is underestimating both how long NAND prices will stay strong and how big Kioxia’s cost advantage really is.

4
00:00:23,743 --> 00:00:31,684
Guest: The analyst sees the stock as undervalued, with a price target of ¥79, 000, which is about 30% above where it trades.

5
00:00:32,044 --> 00:00:38,267
Host: So the core question is whether NAND flash memory prices have peaked or still have room to run. What does the report say?

6
00:00:38,627 --> 00:00:47,636
Guest: It says no, peak is not here yet. The analyst expects NAND prices to rise quarter over quarter for the next six quarters, with the peak coming around Q3 2027.

7
00:00:47,996 --> 00:00:54,312
Guest: That’s about 18 months from now. The key driver is AI inference demand, which is changing the role of NAND memory.

8
00:00:54,672 --> 00:01:00,013
Host: How is AI changing things? I thought NAND was mainly for storage in PCs and phones.

9
00:01:00,373 --> 00:01:07,757
Guest: That’s the traditional view. But the report argues that for AI inference, NAND is becoming part of the core computing system, similar to DRAM.

10
00:01:08,117 --> 00:01:15,593
Guest: Because you need to retain user chat history and context, NAND demand is becoming structural, not just cyclical. And with supply growth constrained,

11
00:01:15,953 --> 00:01:17,207
Host: the market stays tight.

12
00:01:17,567 --> 00:01:22,165
Host: So supply is limited. What about Kioxia specifically? What gives them an edge?

13
00:01:22,525 --> 00:01:28,655
Guest: The report highlights a unique cost advantage. While competitors like Samsung and SK Hynix focus on vertical stacking,

14
00:01:29,015 --> 00:01:39,185
Guest: Kioxia has prioritized horizontal miniaturization. This lets them keep wafer costs much lower—about $2, 000 per wafer versus $4, 000 to $6, 000 for peers.

15
00:01:39,545 --> 00:01:42,564
Host: That translates into a 10-20% bit cost advantage.

16
00:01:42,924 --> 00:01:45,385
Host: And that cost advantage shows up in their margins?

17
00:01:45,745 --> 00:01:53,733
Guest: Exactly. Kioxia has maintained the highest operating margin in the industry since 2022. The analyst thinks this isn’t fully priced in,

18
00:01:54,093 --> 00:01:59,712
Guest: because investors tend to focus on simple specs like layer count, which doesn’t capture Kioxia’s real strength.

19
00:02:00,072 --> 00:02:05,413
Host: That’s a pretty compelling narrative. But what about the risks or the things the report leaves open?

20
00:02:05,773 --> 00:02:13,714
Guest: Good question. The report acknowledges that beyond 2027, when the industry moves to 332-layer and 400-layer technology,

21
00:02:14,074 --> 00:02:20,622
Guest: it’s uncertain whether Kioxia’s lateral scaling advantage will persist. Also, while the demand story from AI is strong,

22
00:02:20,982 --> 00:02:25,951
Host: there’s always the risk of supply-demand imbalances in NAND, which is more volatile than DRAM.

23
00:02:26,311 --> 00:02:32,998
Host: So the report is bullish, but not without nuance. Is there something you’d point people to in the full report for a deeper dive?

24
00:02:33,358 --> 00:02:41,764
Guest: Definitely. The report has a detailed breakdown of how Kioxia achieves its cost advantage, including its use of CBA technology and joint ventures.

25
00:02:42,124 --> 00:02:49,136
Guest: It also includes a scenario analysis with upside and downside cases. That’s worth reading if you want to understand the full range of outcomes.

26
00:02:49,496 --> 00:02:57,298
Host: Great. So to wrap up: the thesis is that NAND prices haven’t peaked, Kioxia’s cost edge is undervalued,

27
00:02:57,658 --> 00:03:04,299
Host: and the full report has the technical details to back it up. For anyone who wants to dig deeper, the full analysis is available.

28
00:03:04,659 --> 00:03:11,300
Guest: Exactly. It’s a strong framework for understanding the NAND cycle and Kioxia’s position. We’ll be watching how the market responds.
